The documentation of coole
--------------------------

coole is a console text editor, a continuation of cooledit.  The
top-level README.md says what it does and how to start it.

This directory holds:

* INSTALL
    What is needed to build coole, the configure options, and how to
    build and install it.  The file INSTALL at the top of the tree
    points here.

* HACKING
    How the source is laid out, how it is formatted, and some
    programming tips.

* FAQ
    Frequently asked questions: keys, the mouse, colors, the terminal,
    editing and the configuration files.

* PLUGINS
    How to write an editor plugin: the API in lib/editor-plugin.h, how
    plugins are loaded, and a minimal example.

* LUA_PLUGINS.md, LUA_API_REFERENCE.md, lua-api.json
    The Lua scripts that the Lua runtime plugin runs in the editor:
    how to write one, and the reference of the API they see.  These are
    installed into the documentation directory.

* man/
    The manual page, coole.1, and its translations.  The page is
    written in markdown (coole.md); the roff under roff/ is made from
    it by maint/update-man-in.sh.

* hlp/
    The help the program shows on F1, which is the markdown of the
    manual page.

* COPYING
    The GNU General Public License, version 3.


Reporting problems
------------------

Report bugs in coole on its issue tracker:

https://github.com/blue-panels/coole/issues

Include the output of "coole --version", the operating system and the
distribution (if applicable) you are using, the compiler and the
configure flags used to compile the program (if you know them;
"coole --configure-options" prints them).

If the program crashed and produced a core dump, please provide a
stack trace of the program.

You can do this by running gdb like this:

gdb coole core
(gdb) where
